+/**
+ * inbox.ts -- shot "The Inbox, one item at a time": the window's Inbox, sidebar folded, its list grouped by plan beside a settled item read in the pane.
+ *
+ * Throwaway (`README.md`). SPEC row 5: the sidebar folded so the Inbox's
+ * list and pane fill the window; the list grouped by plan, "Teammate
+ * invitations" holding four items from its two coding agents (two waiting
+ * on Dean, with the blue dot and the bold title, and two he answered), and
+ * "Usage-based billing", "Webhook retries", and "Onboarding checklist" three
+ * each from a finished agent of their own (one onboarding question still
+ * waiting, the rest settled), so the list runs most of the window's height;
+ * the pane on 0.12.0's "Invite links expire after 7 days or 14?", now
+ * answered: 7 days
+ * marked as Dean's pick, 14 days stepped back, and Dean's reply bubble with
+ * what he did, when, and that it was sent to the agent. The Inbox is opened
+ * and the item chosen by one step, as the home page's row does it, since
+ * the Inbox stands on the first item waiting where nothing is chosen. Each
+ * plan's inbox is answered once from its start and held after, since the
+ * chosen plan's own read asks again as soon as an answer lands; the code
+ * block's lines are answered through `PLANNING_FILE`, and the waiting
+ * question's picture through `CODING_AGENTS_INBOX_ATTACHMENT`.
+ */
+
